    "id": "UgwsR_-yuut2iqwQ3QJ4AaABAg",
    "parent": "root",
    "text": "I got a similar set up running and it's great. One thing I do when I come across stuff like this, is share it to my agent and ask it to review the content for any bits that it may find worth implementing. It's basically telling your AI to go read self-help books. You review what it comes back with, but yeah... at some point the AI will have a different idea of how to arrange it to suit it's own capabilities.\n\nAlready we  have model specific harness needs. I can trust Sol to generally update the log files I got going, but Luna sometimes forgets. Then I wonder, do I run a hook for auto-agentic documentation updates or just depend on running higher models? Hooks are great, but then I'm further tied to Codex for the agent to run how I want. I don't know. It's like the next level up of problems once you have your AIOS or agent or second brain or whatever you want to call it.",
